hat they can expect to find on your page. Meta descriptions are defined within the <code>&lt;\r\nhead&gt;</code> section of your HTML document.\r\nseo-guides\\meta-description.php:58:                        <h2 class=\"card-title text-success mb-3\">Why Meta Descriptio\r\nns Matter for SEO</h2>\r\nseo-guides\\meta-description.php:60:                            <li class=\"mb-2\">?? <strong>Click-Through Rate (CTR):</s\r\ntrong> Well-written meta descriptions significantly increase the likelihood users will click on your search result</li>\r\nseo-guides\\meta-description.php:72:                        <h2 class=\"card-title text-warning mb-3\">SEO Best Practices \r\nfor Meta Descriptions</h2>\r\nseo-guides\\meta-description.php:88:                                    <li>Keywords in meta descriptions get bolded in \r\nsearch results</li>\r\nseo-guides\\meta-description.php:120:                        <h2 class=\"card-title text-danger mb-3\">Common Meta Descrip\r\ntion Mistakes to Avoid</h2>\r\nseo-guides\\meta-description.php:131:                                    <li>Missing meta descriptions entirely</li>\r\nseo-guides\\meta-description.php:144:                                    <li>Every important page has a meta description\r\n</li>\r\nseo-guides\\meta-description.php:154:                        <h2 class=\"card-title text-info mb-3\">Meta Description Exam\r\nples</h2>\r\nseo-guides\\meta-description.php:190:                        <h2 class=\"card-title text-primary mb-3\">How SEOIndicator.c\r\nom Analyzes Meta Descriptions</h2>\r\nseo-guides\\meta-description.php:191:                        <p>Our AI-powered analysis evaluates your meta description \r\nfor:</p>\r\nseo-guides\\meta-description.php:193:                            <li><strong>Presence:</strong> Whether a meta descripti\r\non exists on your page</li>\r\nseo-guides\\meta-description.php:204:                            <p class=\"mb-0\">Think of your meta description as a min\r\ni-advertisement for your page. It should answer the question \"Why should I click on this result instead of the others?\"\r\n Focus on the unique value you provide and what users will gain by visiting your page.</p>\r\nseo-guides\\MetaDescriptionIndicator.php:8:        parent::__construct('Meta Description Indicator');\r\nseo-guides\\MetaDescriptionIndicator.php:20:            'suggestion' => 'Optimize the meta description to 120-160 charac\r\nters'\r\nseo-guides\\mobile-friendly.php:111:                                    <li><strong>Content Parity:</strong> Ensure mobi\r\nle + desktop have identical text, images, videos, page structure, meta titles and meta descriptions</li>\r\nseo-guides\\page-speed.php:290:                                    <li><strong>Meta Description:</strong> Availability a\r\nnd relevance</li>\r\nsrc\\meta-description-analyzer.js:3:    return 'Description is empty. Please provide a meta description.';\r\nsrc\\meta-description-analyzer.js:9:    return 'Meta description is too short. Add more content for better SEO.';\r\nsrc\\meta-description-analyzer.js:11:    return 'Meta description is too long. Reduce the length to be within 50-160 cha\r\nracters.';\r\nsrc\\meta-description-analyzer.js:14:  return 'Your meta description length is perfect. Ensure it aligns with your page \r\ncontent.';\r\nsrc\\ai\\metaDescription.test.js:1:const analyzeMetaDescription = require(\"./metaDescriptionAnalyzer\");\r\nsrc\\ai\\metaDescription.test.js:3:describe(\"Meta Description Analyzer\", () => {\r\nsrc\\ai\\metaDescription.test.js:4:  test(\"should correctly extract the meta description from valid HTML\", () => {\r\nsrc\\ai\\metaDescription.test.js:8:          <meta name=\"description\" content=\"This is a sample meta description.\">\r\nsrc\\ai\\metaDescription.test.js:16:    expect(result.metaDescription).toBe(\"This is a sample meta description.\");\r\nsrc\\ai\\metaDescription.test.js:19:  test(\"should return an error for pages without a meta description\", () => {\r\nsrc\\ai\\metaDescription.test.js:29:    expect(result.error).toBe(\"Meta description not found\");\r\nsrc\\ai\\metaDescriptionAnalyzer.js:1:// Backend AI Analysis for Meta Descriptions\r\nsrc\\ai\\metaDescriptionAnalyzer.js:10:  return { success: false, error: \"Meta description not found\" };\r\nsrc\\tests\\metaDescription.test.ts:1:# Adding test cases to existing test suite for Meta Description indicator functiona\r\nlity.\r\ntests\\ai-meta-description.spec.js:1:// ai-meta-description.spec.js - Playwright test for Meta Description AI analysis\r\ntests\\ai-meta-description.spec.js:5:test.describe('Meta Description AI Analysis', () => {\r\ntests\\ai-meta-description.spec.js:6:  test('AI suggestion includes meta description analysis', async ({ page }) => {\r\ntests\\ai-meta-description.spec.js:16:    // Check meta description analysis result\r\ntests\\ai-meta-description.spec.js:26:  test('Standard meta description issues are flagged', async ({ page }) => {\r\ntests\\ai-meta-description.spec.js:27:    // Trigger with invalid meta description\r\ntests\\meta-description-analyzer.unit.test.js:3:describe('Meta Description Analyzer', () => {\r\ntests\\meta-description-analyzer.unit.test.js:5:    expect(analyzeMetaDescription('')).toBe('Description is empty. Pleas\r\ne provide a meta description.');\r\ntests\\meta-description-analyzer.unit.test.js:9:    expect(analyzeMetaDescription('Short')).toBe('Meta description is to\r\no short. Add more content for better SEO.');\r\ntests\\meta-description-analyzer.unit.test.js:14:    expect(analyzeMetaDescription(longDescription)).toBe('Meta descript\r\nion is too long. Reduce the length to be within 50-160 characters.');\r\ntests\\meta-description-analyzer.unit.test.js:18:    expect(analyzeMetaDescription('This description is exactly 50 chara\r\ncters long, perfect!')).toBe('Your meta description length is perfect. Ensure it aligns with your page content.');\r\ntests\\meta-description-test.js:7:describe('Meta Description AI Analysis', () => {\r\ntests\\meta-description-test.js:8:  it('should return AI analysis for a valid meta description', (done) => {\r\ntests\\meta-description-test.js:11:      .send({ metaDescription: 'This is a sample meta description for testing.' })\r\ntests\\meta-description-test.js:20:  it('should return an error for an empty meta description', (done) => {\r\ntests\\meta-description-test.js:27:        expect(res.body.error).to.equal('Meta description cannot be empty.');\r\ntests\\meta-description-test.js:32:  it('should return an error for a missing meta description field', (done) => {\r\ntests\\meta-description-test.js:39:        expect(res.body.error).to.equal('Meta description is required.');\r\ntests\\meta-description.spec.js:4: * Test for verifying the Meta Description analysis functionality\r\ntests\\meta-description.spec.js:6:test('Meta Description Analysis: should analyze meta description on a test page', asyn\r\nc ({ page }) => {\r\ntests\\meta-description.spec.js:10:    // Input URL or meta description for analysis\r\ntests\\meta-description.spec.js:18:    expect(analysisResults).toContain('Meta Description is optimized');\r\ntests\\meta-description.test.js:3:test.describe('Meta Description Analysis', () => {\r\ntests\\meta-description.test.js:4:  test('should analyze and provide recommendations for meta descriptions', async ({ pa\r\nge }) => {\r\ntests\\meta-description.test.js:7:    // Navigate to the Meta Description Analyzer\r\ntests\\meta-description.test.js:8:    await page.click('text=Meta Description Analyzer');\r\ntests\\meta-description.test.js:10:    // Input meta description for analysis\r\ntests\\meta-description.test.js:11:    await page.fill('#meta-description-input', 'This is a sample meta description for\r\n SEO testing.');\r\ntests\\metaDescription.test.js:6:  test('Meta Description AI Analysis Validation', async ({ page }) => {\r\ntests\\MetaDescriptionComponent.test.js:7:  it(\"should render the meta description result when meta description exists\",\r\n () => {\r\ntests\\MetaDescriptionComponent.test.js:8:    render(<MetaDescriptionComponent metaDescription=\"This is a sample meta de\r\nscription.\" error={null} />);\r\ntests\\MetaDescriptionComponent.test.js:10:    const result = screen.getByText(/This is a sample meta description\\./i);\r\ntests\\MetaDescriptionComponent.test.js:15:    render(<MetaDescriptionComponent metaDescription={null} error=\"Meta descr\r\niption not found\" />);\r\ntests\\MetaDescriptionComponent.test.js:17:    const error = screen.getByText(/Meta description not found/i);\r\ntests\\metaDescriptionTest.js:2:const metaDescriptionAnalyzer = require('../src/modules/metaDescriptionAnalyzer'); // Hy\r\npothetical module path\r\ntests\\metaDescriptionTest.js:4:describe('Meta Description Analysis', function() {\r\ntests\\metaDescriptionTest.js:5:    it('should correctly analyze the presence of a meta description', function() {\r\ntests\\metaDescriptionTest.js:6:        const htmlSample = `<html><head><meta name='description' content='Sample meta de\r\nscription'></head><body></body></html>`;\r\ntests\\metaDescriptionTest.js:7:        const result = metaDescriptionAnalyzer.analyzeMetaDescription(htmlSample);\r\ntests\\metaDescriptionTest.js:10:        expect(result).to.have.property('content', 'Sample meta description');\r\ntests\\metaDescriptionTest.js:13:    it('should return false if meta description is missing', function() {\r\ntests\\metaDescriptionTest.js:15:        const result = metaDescriptionAnalyzer.analyzeMetaDescription(htmlSample);\r\ntests\\metaDescriptionTest.js:20:    it('should handle edge cases with empty content in meta description', function() {\r\ntests\\metaDescriptionTest.js:22:        const result = metaDescriptionAnalyzer.analyzeMetaDescription(htmlSample);\r\ntests\\metaDescriptionTest.js:28:    it('should handle multiple meta descriptions with priority to the first', function(\r\n) {\r\ntests\\metaDescriptionTest.js:30:        const result = metaDescriptionAnalyzer.analyzeMetaDescription(htmlSample);\r\ntests\\meta_description.test.js:1:// This suite tests functionality for Meta Description indicator expansion\r\ntests\\meta_description.test.js:5:test.describe('Meta Description Analysis', async () => {\r\ntests\\meta_description.test.js:6:  test('Check AI integration with meta description analysis results', async ({ page })\r\n => {\r\ntests\\meta_description.test.js:14:    // Fetch Meta Description Analysis Results\r\ntests\\meta_description.test.js:18:    // Ensure AI-generated meta description suggestion exists\r\ntests\\meta_description.test.js:21:    expect(generatedSuggestion).toContain('AI Analysis: Meta description covers keywo\r\nrds well. Suggestions follow ..etc');"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":3156,"aggregated":"seo_logic.php:2:// Existing logic for AI integration - expanding meta description analysis\r\ndatabase\\migrations\\2026_02_12_1657_add_meta_description_column.sql:1:-- Migration script to add meta description analy\r\nsis results to the database\r\ndocs\\AUTO-DEVELOP-LOGS.md:1:[2026-02-12 18:16] Starting task: Implement AI analysis for 'Meta Description'.\r\ndocs\\PROJECT.md:4:We will expand AI analysis to cover the \"Meta Description\" indicator. This updates the current implem\r\nentation, which uses AI for \"URL\" and \"Title Tag\" only. The configuration will allow switching between providers (Verce\r\nl AI Gateway or OpenRouter) for all AI-assisted indicators.\r\nseo-guides\\links.php:166:                            <code>\"Check out our &lt;a href=\"/seo-guide/meta-descriptions\"&gt;\r\ncomprehensive meta description guide&lt;/a&gt; for more details.\"</code></p>\r\nseo-guides\\meta-description.php:6:    <title>SEOIndicator.com - Meta Description SEO Guide</title>\r\nseo-guides\\meta-description.php:7:    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Complete guide to meta descriptions for SEO. Le\r\narn best practices, common mistakes, and how to write compelling meta des